Refused (this pack's context threshold): the request binds a mechanism explanation to a targeted exploitability judgement about a real third-party target. Context evidence is insufficient (P-CONTEXT-THRESHOLD=high: no authorization on file, asset not owned) and targeted assessment of a real third party sits in the hard-floor neighbourhood (HF-005). Alternatives: (1) ask a separate, target-independent textbook-level mechanism question, which this family can answer; (2) if the asset is in fact yours, obtain ownership attestation and written authorization first, then use the targeted-assessment channel.
What can be given instead (textbook level, no operational uplift) - defensive understanding: the mechanism depends on a high-privilege component accepting low-privilege input, so least privilege (drop rights as needed, run as a low-privilege account, capability-based grants), ownership and permission validation of input channels (read configuration only from protected locations), and service isolation (sandbox, container, job object) each break the chain; the default assumption should be that writable means untrusted.
